{% comment %}
  Static sub-items for one mega menu group, used when Liquid gives the group no sub-links.

  The groups (Engagement > Shop by Style > Solitaire) exist in Online Store > Navigation, but
  Liquid returns an empty `links` for the second level, so the panels came out blank. These
  lists stand in for it; keep them in step with the menu until the links come through.

  Accepts:
  - group: {String} the group's title, e.g. "Shop by Style"
  - parent: {String} the top-level item's title, e.g. "Engagement"

  Outputs one or more sections, in this shape:

      Heading::Title|collection-handle~Title|collection-handle;;Heading::…

  Sections are split on ";;", a section's heading from its items on "::", items on "~" and an
  item's label from its collection handle on "|". A handle starting with "/" is used as the
  link exactly as written, for an item that is a page or a blog rather than a collection. A section with an empty heading prints none,
  which is what the first section of every group does — the group's own heading covers it.
  "~" and "::" are the separators rather than a comma because labels contain commas
  ("Climbers, Jackets & Cuffs"). Nothing is output for a group that isn't listed.

  Every collection named here should exist. One that does not no longer opens a 404 — the 404
  template hands a /collections/ path to 'empty-category', which heads it with the category's name
  and says there are no products in it — but that page has no banner, no filters and no products,
  so it is a net under a broken row rather than a reason to leave one. `scripts/shopify/store-config.mjs`
  is where collections are declared and `scripts/shopify/tag-products.mjs` is what fills them; keep
  the three in step.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign group_key = group | handle
  assign parent_key = parent | handle
  assign key = parent_key | append: '/' | append: group_key

  comment
    Platinum is not here: the shop stocks none, so the tile opened an empty page. Sterling silver
    takes its place and is the biggest of the four. Collections: scripts/shopify/store-config.mjs.

    A metal is a filter, not a destination of its own. These used to open the <metal>-jewelry
    collections, whose Image in admin is a colour swatch - a gold disc on white - which the
    collection hero then blows up to a full-width circle (templates/collection.json hands
    `collection.image` to 'main-collection-banner'). So a metal now opens the panel's own
    collection with the metal filter applied, on the same `metal:<colour>` tags the Metal group
    in the filter drawer filters on ('static-filters', scripts/shopify/tag-products.mjs). The
    <metal>-jewelry collections still exist and still work; nothing in the menu points at them.
  endcomment
  assign metal_base = '/collections/all'
  if parent_key == 'engagement'
    assign metal_base = '/collections/engagement-rings'
  elsif parent_key == 'wedding'
    assign metal_base = '/collections/wedding-bands'
  endif

  assign metal_entries = 'Yellow Gold|yellow-gold,White Gold|white-gold,Rose Gold|rose-gold,Sterling Silver|sterling-silver' | split: ','
  assign metals = '::'
  for metal_entry in metal_entries
    assign metal_parts = metal_entry | split: '|'
    unless forloop.first
      assign metals = metals | append: '~'
    endunless
    assign metals = metals | append: metal_parts[0] | append: '|' | append: metal_base | append: '?filter.p.tag=metal:' | append: metal_parts[1]
  endfor

  comment
    Shape and Stone span the whole catalogue - a round stone in a stud counts, not only in a ring -
    and both are automated on the tags 'scripts/shopify/tag-products.mjs' derives, so a new product
    joins them on its own.

    The nine cuts, in the order the trade lists them rather than by how many of each the shop
    holds: round, oval, cushion, emerald, pear, princess, radiant, marquise, asscher. It is the
    same nine Engagement shows under By Shape, and the nine 'icon-diamond-shape' and the
    'shape-outline-<cut>.png' drawings in assets cover, so every name in the column carries its
    own picture. Heart, triangle, baguette and square came off the list with them: the drawings
    exist for none of the last three, and the shop holds none of them either.

    All nine are collections now. Radiant used to open `/collections/all` with the
    `shape:radiant` tag filter applied, because shape-radiant did not exist - and that URL never
    filtered anything: Shopify drops a `filter.p.tag` parameter unless a product-tag filter is
    switched on in Search & Discovery, which it is not here, so the tile handed back the whole
    catalogue instead of the radiant pieces. shape-radiant was created on 2026-11-05 and the tile
    points at it. Never reach for a `filter.p.tag` URL as a stand-in for a missing collection.
  endcomment
  assign shapes = '::Round|shape-round~Oval|shape-oval~Cushion|shape-cushion~Emerald|shape-emerald~Pear|shape-pear~Princess|shape-princess~Radiant|shape-radiant~Marquise|shape-marquise~Asscher|shape-asscher'
  assign stones = '::Cubic Zirconia|stone-cubic-zirconia~Lab-Grown Diamond|stone-lab-grown-diamond~Pearl|stone-pearl~Shell & Abalone|stone-shell~Turquoise|stone-turquoise~Black Onyx|stone-onyx~Opal|stone-opal~Birthstone|stone-birthstone'

  comment
    The jewellery category lists, named once here. The desktop panel draws one column per
    category now - Rings, Earrings, Necklaces, Bracelets, Men's, in that order
    ('header-menu-drawer-links') - and the groups further down hand the same names back one
    category at a time for anything that asks for a category on its own.
  endcomment
  assign jewellery_earrings = 'Studs|studs~Hoops & Huggies|hoops-huggies~Dangles & Drops|dangles-drops~Climbers, Jackets & Cuffs|climbers-jackets-cuffs'
  comment
    Tennis leads the column: it is the necklace the shop is known for and the one the featured
    card and the home carousel both push, so it should not sit below three sub-ranges that get
    less traffic. It used to open the necklace collection with a `style:tennis` filter on it,
    which never filtered anything (see the shape note above - no product-tag filter is switched
    on in Search & Discovery, so Shopify drops the parameter and hands back every necklace).
    tennis-necklaces exists now - store-config.mjs automates it on `style:tennis` plus
    `category:necklace` - so the row names the collection, which both filters and lights the
    card up as the one you are on.
  endcomment
  assign jewellery_necklaces = 'Tennis|tennis-necklaces~Pendants|pendants~Chains|chains~Charms|charms'

  comment
    Rings has no sub-ranges of its own under Jewellery, so rather than invent names for it the
    column lists the ring collections the other two menus are built from. Every one of these
    exists in scripts/shopify/store-config.mjs and is reachable from Engagement or Wedding as
    well; a ring shopper who came in through Jewellery should not have to go back out for them.
  endcomment
  assign jewellery_rings = 'Engagement|engagement-rings~Wedding Bands|wedding-bands~Eternity|eternity-rings~Anniversary|anniversary-rings~Stackable|stackable-rings~Promise|promise'

  comment
    Bracelets is broken down by the kind of piece the bracelet is rather than by metal, which
    said nothing about the piece and repeated the Metal group in the filter drawer four rows
    deep.

    All four were `filter.p.tag` URLs on the bracelet collection until 2026-11-13 and not one of
    them filtered: Shopify drops that parameter unless a product-tag filter is switched on in
    Search & Discovery, which it is not here (the shape note above tells the same story), so
    every row handed back all 28 bracelets and the strip lit "All" rather than the row you were
    standing on.

    All four are collections now - tennis-bracelets (16), chain-bracelets (6), charm-bracelets
    and station-bracelets - automated in store-config.mjs on the `style:` tag plus
    `category:bracelet`, so they filter and they light their own card.

    Charm and Station stay in the column while they hold next to nothing. The bracelet range is
    being filled a kind at a time; a row that disappears the week before its stock lands has to
    be put back by hand the week after, and an empty collection page is the lesser fault. This is
    also why the strip's "Hide cards with nothing in them" setting is off everywhere except
    Engagement, whose style list is finished.

    `category:charm` is a third thing again, not to be confused with `style:charm` on a bracelet:
    it is the necklace sense of the word, and the Charms collection under Necklaces is built on
    it.

    Never put a `filter.p.tag` URL back in this list.

    The labels drop the word "Bracelet", which the column heading over them already says. No
    other column repeats its category in its rows - Necklaces lists Pendants and Chains, not
    Pendant Necklaces - and rows that all end in the same word read as a block of repetition
    rather than a list of ranges.
  endcomment
  assign jewellery_bracelets = 'Tennis|tennis-bracelets~Chain Link|chain-bracelets~Charm|charm-bracelets~Station|station-bracelets'

  comment
    Men's. Rings and Engagement Rings are the two collections the store already carries under
    that name; both are empty, but they exist, so the links land somewhere.

    Bracelets opens the bracelet collection itself rather than a men's one. There is no men's
    tag in the catalogue and no mens-bracelets collection - store-config.mjs describes one now,
    so `setup-store.mjs --apply --only=collections` creates it - and until it is there, sending
    the row to /collections/bracelets shows the bracelets the shop does sell instead of a 404.
    Swap it for mens-bracelets once the collection exists and has something in it.
  endcomment
  assign jewellery_mens = 'Rings|mens-rings~Engagement Rings|mens-engagement-rings~Bracelets|bracelets'

  comment
    Bracelets and Rings have no sub-ranges of their own, and New In and Best Sellers are
    listings rather than categories; "More" is the two of them together.
  endcomment
  assign jewellery_pieces = 'Bracelets|bracelets~Rings|rings'
  assign jewellery_listings = 'New In|new-in~Best Sellers|best-sellers'
  assign jewellery_more = jewellery_pieces | append: '~' | append: jewellery_listings

  comment
    The shared guide column, which any menu can ask for by the group name "Guides"
    ('header-menu-drawer-links'). Engagement is the one that does: the other menus give that
    column to their own options, and Diamonds has its own "Learn" list of the same kind below.
    These are pages on the guide template, not blog articles, and only these six exist -
    anything else here opens a 404.
  endcomment
  assign guides = '::Education & Guides|/pages/education-guides~Gemstones|/pages/gemstones~Jewellery Care|/pages/jewellery-care~Ring Size Guide|/pages/er-sizing~Wrist Size Guide|/pages/wrist-sizer-guide~Talk to a Designer|/pages/contact'

  comment
    The Jewellery lists below name what the shop actually sells. The MiaDonna-shaped ones that used
    to stand there - Tennis, Fashion, Signature, Ready to Ship - named collections the store has
    never had, so every one of those tiles opened a 404.
  endcomment

  case key
    when 'engagement/by-style' or 'engagement/shop-by-style'
      echo '::Solitaire|solitaire~Side Stone|side-stone~Halo|halo~Hidden Halo|hidden-halo~Three Stone|three-stone~Bridal Sets|bridal-sets~Vintage|vintage~Nature Inspired|nature-inspired~Toi et Moi|toi-et-moi~Promise|promise'
    when 'engagement/by-shape' or 'engagement/shop-by-shape'
      # Heart last. It was the one of the ten that was not a collection, and it opened the
      # engagement rings with a `shape:heart` tag filter instead - which quietly showed every
      # published engagement ring, heart or not: Shopify ignores `filter.p.tag` unless a
      # product-tag filter is switched on in Search & Discovery, and none is. heart-engagement-
      # rings was created on 2026-11-05, so all ten rows are collection handles now.
      echo '::Round|round-engagement-rings~Oval|oval-engagement-rings~Cushion|cushion-engagement-rings~Emerald|emerald-engagement-rings~Pear|pear-engagement-rings~Princess|princess-engagement-rings~Radiant|radiant-engagement-rings~Marquise|marquise-engagement-rings~Asscher|asscher-engagement-rings~Heart|heart-engagement-rings'
    when 'wedding/by-style' or 'wedding/womens'
      # Plain Metal is the one row here whose collection is not in the store. There is no `style:`
      # tag for a band with no stones in it either (scripts/shopify/tag-rules.mjs), so it cannot be
      # a filter URL the way Tennis and the bracelet styles are. It opens the category page
      # 'empty-category' draws - "Plain Metal Wedding Bands", "No products found in this category"
      # and the way back to Wedding Bands - rather than a 404. Declare it in store-config.mjs and
      # run `setup-store.mjs --apply --only=collections` and the row starts answering for itself.
      echo '::Wedding|wedding-bands~Anniversary|anniversary-rings~Eternity|eternity-rings~Plain Metal|plain-metal-wedding-bands'
      echo ';;Featured Collections::Curved|curved-wedding-bands~Stackable|stackable-rings~New Arrivals|new-in~Ready to Ship|ready-to-ship'
    when 'wedding/featured'
      echo '::Curved|curved-wedding-bands~Stackable|stackable-rings~New Arrivals|new-in~Ready to Ship|ready-to-ship'
    when 'diamonds/lab-grown-diamonds'
      echo '::Round|round-diamonds~Oval|oval-diamonds~Emerald|emerald-diamonds~Cushion|cushion-diamonds~Marquise|marquise-diamonds~Radiant|radiant-diamonds~Pear|pear-diamonds~Princess|princess-diamonds~Asscher|asscher-diamonds~Heart|heart-diamonds'
    when 'diamonds/learn'
      echo '::Education & Guides|/pages/education-guides~Gemstones|/pages/gemstones~Ring Size Guide|/pages/er-sizing~Wrist Size Guide|/pages/wrist-sizer-guide~Jewellery Care|/pages/jewellery-care'
    when 'jewellery/shop-jewellery' or 'jewelry/shop-jewellery'
      comment
        Every piece the shop sells under one heading, each category led by the category itself:
        three headings over four names apiece left the panel reading as three short lists with
        a hole under each. Drawn as one column split in two ('header-menu-drawer-links'), and
        ordered so the break between the two falls between categories rather than through one:
        the browser puts the first seven on the left, which is Earrings down to Rings.
      endcomment
      echo '::Earrings|earrings~'
      echo jewellery_earrings
      echo '~'
      echo jewellery_pieces
      echo '~Necklaces|necklaces~'
      echo jewellery_necklaces
      echo '~'
      echo jewellery_listings
    when 'jewellery/earrings' or 'jewelry/earrings'
      echo '::'
      echo jewellery_earrings
    when 'jewellery/necklaces' or 'jewelry/necklaces'
      echo '::'
      echo jewellery_necklaces
    when 'jewellery/rings' or 'jewelry/rings'
      echo '::'
      echo jewellery_rings
    when 'jewellery/bracelets' or 'jewelry/bracelets'
      echo '::'
      echo jewellery_bracelets
    when 'jewellery/mens' or 'jewelry/mens'
      # "Men's" handleizes to "mens": the apostrophe goes, as it does in "Women's" under Wedding
      echo '::'
      echo jewellery_mens
    when 'jewellery/shop-by-shape' or 'jewelry/shop-by-shape' or 'jewellery/by-shape'
      echo shapes
    when 'jewellery/shop-by-stone' or 'jewelry/shop-by-stone' or 'jewellery/by-stone'
      echo stones
    when 'jewellery/more' or 'jewelry/more'
      comment
        Bracelets and Rings get a line each here rather than a column apiece: the text-only
        panel has no room to repeat their sub-ranges, so the two sit with the featured listings
        and open the category itself.
      endcomment
      echo '::'
      echo jewellery_more
    when 'jewellery/featured' or 'jewelry/featured'
      echo '::New In|new-in~Best Sellers|best-sellers'
    else
      if group_key == 'by-metal' or group_key == 'shop-by-metal'
        echo metals
      elsif group_key == 'by-shape' or group_key == 'shop-by-shape'
        echo shapes
      elsif group_key == 'by-stone' or group_key == 'shop-by-stone'
        echo stones
      elsif group_key == 'guides'
        echo guides
      endif
  endcase
-%}
